# Add ClinicalTrials.gov Data Source Integration

## Goal Description
The project currently lists ClinicalTrials.gov only as a visual placeholder. This plan details how to fetch, store, and display real trial data, enriching pharmacovigilance insights by combining pre‑market trial results with post‑market adverse event reports.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> Review the scope and confirm which trial fields you need (e.g., NCT ID, title, status, results, adverse events). If you prefer a limited subset, let us know so the plan can be trimmed.

## Open Questions
> [!WARNING]
> - Do you want to store trial data in the existing SQLite DB (`pharmawatch.db`) or a separate file?
> - Should the data be refreshed on demand, on a schedule, or both?
> - Which UI components should display trial data (e.g., source meter, detail panel, separate "Trials" tab)?

## Proposed Changes
---
### Backend (Python)
- **[NEW]** `clinicaltrials.py` – module with functions to query the ClinicalTrials.gov API (use the XML/JSON endpoint). Includes:
  - `search_trials(drug_name: str) -> List[Dict]`
  - Helper to parse relevant fields: `nct_id, title, phase, status, results_url, adverse_events`.
- **[MODIFY]** `app.py`
  - Import `clinicaltrials` and add Flask route `GET /api/clinicaltrials?drug=<name>`.
  - Optionally persist results in SQLite (`trials` table) with columns matching parsed fields.
- **[NEW]** Migration script `add_trials_table.sql` to create the `trials` table.
- **[NEW]** Scheduler (simple thread or `APScheduler`) to refresh trials nightly (optional).

---
### Front‑end (JavaScript / HTML)
- **[MODIFY]** `src/app.js`
  - Extend `SOURCE_LABELS` to include `ct: 'ClinicalTrials'` (already present) and add fetch logic when the user selects the ClinicalTrials source.
  - New function `loadClinicalTrials(drug)` that calls `/api/clinicaltrials?drug=` and renders results.
- **[NEW]** UI component `trial-card` (HTML template) showing trial title, phase, status, link to NCT page, and a small adverse‑event summary.
- **[MODIFY]** `index.html`
  - Add a new section/tab "Clinical Trials" under the Sources panel.
  - Insert reference link in the "Key References" list (already present) – keep as is.
  - Update source meter label (already present) to reflect real‑time simulated rate or hide if not needed.
- **[MODIFY]** Signal table filter to include `ct` rows (already uses `SOURCE_LABELS`). Ensure rows now contain real trial data when source = `ct`.

